{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,255p' tests/dist/text.browser.test.ts; rg -n 'textPage|messagesPage|dirty|Messages' tests/dist/pages/sentinels.ts\nsed -n '375,425p' packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts; sed -n '517,546p' packages/axylo/test/core/snapshot.test.ts\nsed -n '1,130p' packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-donut.test.ts; sed -n '40,115p' packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\nrg -n '##|\\\\*\\\\*' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tests-opus.review.md | head -115\"","aggregated_output":"/**\n * Spec DX8: labels and formatter output are inserted as text, never as HTML. Review finding 20: one distinct\n * sentinel per text source and chart type (pages/sentinels.ts), each destination triggered, and for each an\n * exact literal expectation, so one surface cannot vouch for another.\n *\n * Sources: title, subtitle, description (the summary), series name, category, x and y field labels, unit,\n * x and y value formatters, tick formatters, every built-in message that reaches the page, the reader note on\n * the dirty input, and author error text. Destinations: heading, accessible name and description, legend,\n * axis ticks and titles, tooltip or readout, table caption, headers and cells, and `aria-valuetext`.\n *\n * Each sentinel is `<u data-axs=\"id\">body</u>`. Parsed, it would become a `u` element with `data-axs`: the\n * page's observer (pages/observe.js) records any such element and the test counts them. Read as text, it must\n * appear character for character; every `data-axs` the page shows must belong to a whole sentinel, so a\n * truncated, escaped or half-parsed one fails. The pages are served under the strict policy of\n * csp.browser.test.ts, from the packed script-tag file and from a bundled module.\n */\nimport { afterAll, beforeAll, describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport type { Page } from 'playwright-core';\nimport { bundle, closeBrowser, cspPolicy, drawn, launch, open, startServer, type Server, type Watched } from './browser';\nimport { fixture, here } from './paths';\nimport { KINDS, MESSAGE_CHARTS, S, SOURCES, type Kind } from './pages/sentinels';\n\nlet server: Server;\nconst pages = path.join(here, 'pages');\nconst scripts: Record<string, string> = {};\n\nbeforeAll(async () => {\n  server = await startServer();\n  await launch();\n  for (const [name, fn] of [['sentinel', 'makeSentinelCharts'], ['message', 'makeMessageCharts']] as const) {\n    scripts[`${name}-classic`] = (await bundle({\n      name: `text-${name}-classic`, cwd: pages, contents: `import { ${fn}, type Library } from './sentinels';\\n${fn}((window as unknown as { Axylo: Library }).Axylo);`,\n    })).url;\n    scripts[`${name}-module`] = (await bundle({\n      name: `text-${name}-module`, cwd: fixture('npm'), format: 'esm', conditions: ['development'], allow: [pages],\n      contents: `import * as A from 'axylo';\\nimport { ${fn} } from ${JSON.stringify(path.join(pages, 'sentinels'))};\\n${fn}(A);`,\n    })).url;\n  }\n});\nafterAll(async () => { await closeBrowser(); await server?.close(); });\n\nconst LOADERS = {\n  'script tag, production (axylo.iife.min.js)': (name: string) => `<script src=\"/script/node_modules/axylo/dist/axylo.iife.min.js\"></script><script src=\"${scripts[`${name}-classic`]}\"></script>`,\n  'bundled module, development condition': (name: string) => `<script type=\"module\" src=\"${scripts[`${name}-module`]}\"></script>`,\n};\n\nlet counter = 0;\nasync function load(ids: readonly string[], script: string): Promise<Watched & { id: string }> {\n  const id = `text-${++counter}`;\n  server.pages.set(`/text/${id}.html`, {\n    html: `<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Text</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/pages/page.css\"><script src=\"/pages/observe.js\"></script></head><body>\n${ids.map(c => `<div class=\"${c === 'compact' ? 'tile' : 'chart tall'}\" id=\"${c}\"></div>`).join('\\n')}\n${script}</body></html>`,\n    headers: { 'content-security-policy': cspPolicy(id) },\n  });\n  const w = await open(server);\n  await w.page.goto(`${server.origin}/text/${id}.html`);\n  return { ...w, id };\n}\n\n/** A sentinel with any plain body: the shape formatter output takes. */\nconst anyBody = (sentinelId: string): RegExp => new RegExp(`<u data-axs=\"${sentinelId}\">[^<>]*</u>`);\nconst exactBody = (sentinelId: string, body: RegExp): RegExp => new RegExp(`^<u data-axs=\"${sentinelId}\">${body.source}</u>$`);\n/** What is left of a text once every whole sentinel is removed: must hold no markup at all. */\nconst residue = (text: string): string => text.replace(/<u data-axs=\"[\\w-]+\">[^<>]*<\\/u>/g, '');\n/**\n * True when the text holds only whole sentinels and plain text. The charts are sized so that no sentinel\n * label is truncated (spec L1 would allow an ellipsis): a cut sentinel fails here as a mangled one would.\n */\nconst clean = (text: string): boolean => !/[<>]|data-axs/.test(residue(text));\n\n/** Everything the page shows as text or attribute value, and how many parsed sentinels exist. */\nasync function pageText(page: Page): Promise<{ texts: string[]; attrs: string[]; parsed: number; created: string[] }> {\n  return page.evaluate(() => {\n    const texts: string[] = [];\n    const attrs: string[] = [];\n    // Per element: an axis label's wrapped lines are one text; otherwise each element's own text nodes.\n    for (const el of Array.from(document.body.querySelectorAll('*'))) {\n      for (const a of Array.from(el.attributes)) attrs.push(a.value);\n      if (el.tagName === 'SCRIPT' || el.closest('.axylo-label') && !el.classList.contains('axylo-label')) continue;\n      if (el.classList.contains('axylo-label')) { texts.push(Array.from(el.children).map(l => l.textContent ?? '').join(' ')); continue; }\n      const own = Array.from(el.childNodes).filter(n => n.nodeType === 3).map(n => n.textContent ?? '').join('');\n      if (own) texts.push(own);\n    }\n    return {\n      texts, attrs, parsed: document.querySelectorAll('[data-axs], u').length,\n      created: (window as unknown as { __created: string[] }).__created,\n    };\n  });\n}\n\n/** Text of each element matching `selector` under the chart; axis labels are joined across their wrapped lines. */\nconst textsOf = (page: Page, chart: string, selector: string): Promise<string[]> =>\n  page.evaluate(([c, sel]) => Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(`#${c} ${sel}`)).map(e => {\n    const lines = Array.from(e.children).filter(k => k.tagName === 'DIV');\n    return e.classList.contains('axylo-label') && lines.length > 0 ? lines.map(l => l.textContent ?? '').join(' ') : e.textContent ?? '';\n  }), [chart, selector] as const);\n\n/** The text of the elements an attribute (aria-labelledby, aria-describedby) points at. */\nconst referenced = (page: Page, chart: string, attribute: string): Promise<string> =>\n  page.evaluate(([c, attr]) => {\n    const fig = document.querySelector(`#${c} figure`)!;\n    const ids = fig.getAttribute(attr);\n    if (!ids) return attr === 'aria-labelledby' ? fig.getAttribute('aria-label') ?? '' : '';\n    return ids.split(/\\s+/).map(i => document.getElementById(i)?.textContent ?? '').join(' ');\n  }, [chart, attribute] as const);\n\n/** Moves the pointer over the plot until the visible tooltip or readout contains `anchor`; returns that surface's parts. */\nasync function tooltipWith(page: Page, chart: string, anchor: string): Promise<{ title: string[]; series: string[]; values: string[]; all: string } | null> {\n  const plot = page.locator(`#${chart} .axylo-plot`);\n  await plot.scrollIntoViewIfNeeded();\n  const box = (await plot.boundingBox())!;\n  const surface = page.locator(`#${chart} .axylo-tooltip, #${chart} .axylo-readout`).filter({ visible: true });\n  for (const fy of chart === 'scatter' ? [0.2, 0.35, 0.5, 0.65, 0.8] : [0.5]) {\n    for (let fx = 0.1; fx < 0.98; fx += chart === 'scatter' ? 0.025 : 0.05) {\n      await page.mouse.move(box.x + box.width * fx, box.y + box.height * fy);\n      await page.waitForTimeout(30);\n      if (await surface.count() !== 1) continue;\n      const all = (await surface.textContent()) ?? '';\n      if (!all.includes(anchor)) continue;\n      const part = (cls: string) => surface.locator(cls).allTextContents();\n      return { title: await part('.axylo-tooltip-title'), series: await part('.axylo-tooltip-series'), values: await part('.axylo-tooltip-value'), all };\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\ndescribe.each(Object.entries(LOADERS))('%s', (_label, loader) => {\n  it('every author text source reaches its surfaces literally, on all five chart types and the compact variant', async () => {\n    const w = await load([...KINDS, 'compact'], loader('sentinel'));\n    const page = w.page;\n    for (const kind of KINDS) expect((await drawn(page, `#${kind}`)).marks, `${kind} drawn`).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n\n    for (const kind of KINDS) {\n      const id = SOURCES[kind];\n      const s = (k: string) => S(id[k]!);\n      const at = `${kind}:`;\n      const cartesian = kind !== 'donut';\n      const anchor = cartesian ? s('series') : s('category');\n\n      // Heading, accessible name, subtitle, description.\n      expect(await textsOf(page, kind, '.axylo-title'), `${at} heading`).toEqual([s('title')]);\n      expect(await referenced(page, kind, 'aria-labelledby'), `${at} accessible name`).toBe(s('title'));\n      expect(await textsOf(page, kind, '.axylo-subtitle'), `${at} subtitle`).toEqual([s('subtitle')]);\n      const description = await referenced(page, kind, 'aria-describedby');\n      for (const k of ['description', ...(cartesian ? ['xLabel', 'yLabel', 'series'] : ['category', 'unit'])]) {\n        expect(description, `${at} description carries ${k}`).toContain(s(k));\n      }\n      expect(clean(description), `${at} description: ${residue(description)}`).toBe(true);\n\n      // Legend.\n      if (cartesian) {\n        expect((await textsOf(page, kind, '.axylo-legend-entry .axylo-control-label')).sort(), `${at} legend`).toEqual(['Plain', s('series')].sort());\n      } else {\n        expect(await textsOf(page, kind, '.axylo-legend-name'), `${at} legend names`).toEqual([s('category'), 'Firefox', 'Safari']);\n        const values = await textsOf(page, kind, '.axylo-legend-value');\n        expect(values[0], `${at} legend value`).toContain(S(id.yFormat!, '45'));\n        expect(values[0]).toContain(s('unit'));\n        for (const v of values) expect(clean(v), `${at} legend value ${v}`).toBe(true);\n      }\n\n      // Axis ticks and titles.\n      if (cartesian) {\n        const labels = await textsOf(page, kind, '.axylo-text .axylo-label');\n        for (const tick of ['yTick', 'xTick'].filter(k => id[k])) {\n          const ticks = labels.filter(l => l.includes(`data-axs=\"${id[tick]}\"`));\n          expect(ticks.length, `${at} ${tick} labels`).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);\n          for (const t of ticks) expect(t, `${at} ${tick}`).toMatch(exactBody(id[tick]!, /-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?/));\n        }\n        expect(labels, `${at} x axis title`).toContain(s('xLabel'));\n        const yTitle = labels.find(l => l.includes(s('yLabel')));\n        expect(yTitle, `${at} y axis title`).toBeDefined();\n        expect(yTitle).toContain(s('unit'));\n        for (const l of labels) expect(clean(l), `${at} axis label ${l}`).toBe(true);\n      }\n\n      // Tooltip or readout.\n      const tip = await tooltipWith(page, kind, anchor);\n      expect(tip, `${at} a tooltip showing ${anchor}`).not.toBeNull();\n      expect(tip!.series, `${at} tooltip series`).toContain(anchor);\n      expect(tip!.values.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n      for (const v of tip!.values.filter(x => !/^\\d/.test(x) || x.includes('<'))) {\n        expect(v, `${at} tooltip value`).toMatch(anyBody(id.yFormat!));\n        expect(v).toContain(s('unit'));\n      }\n      if (kind === 'line' || kind === 'area') expect(tip!.title, `${at} tooltip x`).toEqual([expect.stringMatching(exactBody(id.xFormat!, /2026-03-0[2-6]/))]);\n      if (kind === 'bar') expect([s('category'), 'North', 'South'], `${at} tooltip category`).toContain(tip!.title[0]);\n      if (kind === 'donut') expect(tip!.title, `${at} tooltip slice`).toEqual([s('category')]);\n      if (kind === 'scatter') expect(tip!.all, `${at} tooltip x`).toMatch(anyBody(id.xFormat!));\n      expect(clean(tip!.all), `${at} tooltip: ${residue(tip!.all)}`).toBe(true);\n\n      // aria-valuetext of the plot's keyboard proxy, as the pointer left it.\n      const valuetext = (await page.locator(`#${kind} .axylo-proxy`).getAttribute('aria-valuetext')) ?? '';\n      expect(valuetext, `${at} aria-valuetext`).toMatch(anyBody(id.yFormat!));\n      expect(valuetext).toContain(s('unit'));\n      expect(valuetext).toMatch(anyBody(kind === 'donut' || kind === 'bar' ? id.category! : id.xFormat!));\n      expect(clean(valuetext), `${at} aria-valuetext: ${residue(valuetext)}`).toBe(true);\n      await page.mouse.move(1, 1);\n\n      // Table: caption, headers, and each cell against the fixture row it came from.\n      await page.locator(`#${kind} [role=\"toolbar\"] button`, { hasText: 'View as table' }).click();\n      await expect.poll(() => page.locator(`#${kind} table`).count()).toBe(1);\n      expect(await textsOf(page, kind, 'table caption'), `${at} caption`).toEqual([s('title')]);\n      const headers = await textsOf(page, kind, 'thead th');\n      const rows = await page.evaluate(c => Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(`#${c} tbody tr`)).map(r => Array.from(r.children).map(x => x.textContent ?? '')), kind);\n      for (const cell of [...headers, ...rows.flat()]) expect(clean(cell), `${at} table cell ${cell}`).toBe(true);\n      const col = (pred: (h: string) => boolean) => headers.findIndex(pred);\n      const value = (v: number) => S(id.yFormat!, String(v));\n      if (kind === 'line' || kind === 'area' || kind === 'bar') {\n        expect(headers[0], `${at} x header`).toBe(s('xLabel'));\n        const mine = col(h => h.includes(s('series'))), plain = col(h => h.startsWith('Plain'));\n        expect(headers[mine]).toContain(s('unit'));\n        const keys = kind === 'bar' ? [s('category'), 'North', 'South'] : ['2026-03-02', '2026-03-03', '2026-03-04', '2026-03-05', '2026-03-06'].map(d => S(id.xFormat!, d));\n        expect(rows.map(r => r[0]), `${at} row headers`).toEqual(keys);\n        rows.forEach((r, i) => {\n          const base = kind === 'bar' ? 300 + 40 * i : 100 + 10 * i;\n          expect(r[mine], `${at} row ${i}, ${s('series')}`).toContain(value(base));\n          expect(r[plain], `${at} row ${i}, Plain`).toContain(value(base + (kind === 'bar' ? 25 : 50)));\n          expect(r[mine]).toContain(s('unit'));\n        });\n      }\n      if (kind === 'scatter') {\n        expect(headers[0]).toBe(s('xLabel'));\n        const y = col(h => h.includes(s('yLabel')));\n        expect(headers[y]).toContain(s('unit'));\n        const seriesCol = rows[0]!.findIndex((_, j) => j !== 0 && j !== y);\n        rows.forEach((r, i) => {\n          expect(r[0], `${at} row ${i} x`).toBe(S(id.xFormat!, String(10 + 5 * i)));\n          expect(r[y], `${at} row ${i} y`).toContain(value(40 + ((i * 7) % 11) * 3));\n          expect(r[seriesCol], `${at} row ${i} series`).toBe(i % 2 ? s('series') : 'Plain');\n        });\n      }\n      if (kind === 'donut') {\n        const v = col(h => h.includes(s('yLabel')));\n        expect(headers[v]).toContain(s('unit'));\n        expect(rows.map(r => r[0]), `${at} row headers`).toEqual([s('category'), 'Firefox', 'Safari']);\n        expect(rows.map(r => r[v]), `${at} values`).toEqual([expect.stringContaining(value(45)), expect.stringContaining(value(30)), expect.stringContaining(value(25))]);\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Compact: a static image whose name and description are its text (spec 3.7, C1).\n    expect(await page.locator('#compact figure').getAttribute('role')).toBe('img');\n    expect(await referenced(page, 'compact', 'aria-labelledby')).toBe(S('c-title'));\n    expect(await referenced(page, 'compact', 'aria-describedby')).toContain(S('c-desc'));\n\n    const all = await pageText(page);\n    for (const t of [...all.texts, ...all.attrs]) expect(clean(t), `page text: ${residue(t).slice(0, 120)}`).toBe(true);\n    expect(all.parsed, 'parsed sentinels').toBe(0);\n    expect(all.created, 'elements created from text').toEqual([]);\n    expect(w.errors).toEqual([]);\n    expect(server.reports.get(w.id) ?? []).toEqual([]);\n    await w.context.close();\n  });\n\n68:/** Every built-in message key (public Messages): each replaced by its own sentinel on the messages page. */\n79:/** Mon–Sun with a NaN, a stray string and an absent value: the Phase 1 dirty fixture, so the reader note shows. */\n80:const dirty = ['2026-03-02', '2026-03-03', '2026-03-04', '2026-03-05', '2026-03-06', '2026-03-07', '2026-03-08']\n92:    line: A.line('#line', { title: 'Dirty', data: dirty, x: 'day', y: 'value', messages: m }),\n111:  // The reader note on the dirty input with the built-in template and only {seeTable} replaced.\n112:  charts.note = A.line('#note', { title: 'Note', data: dirty, x: 'day', y: 'value', messages: { seeTable: S('m-seeTable') } });\n    const meta = await page.evaluate(() => {\n      const event = new WheelEvent('wheel', { deltaY: -100, metaKey: true, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, clientX: 300, clientY: 200 });\n      document.querySelector('#chart .axylo-plot')!.dispatchEvent(event);\n      return event.defaultPrevented;\n    });\n    expect(meta).toBe(false);\n    await settle(page);\n    expect(await domain(page)).toEqual(full);\n    await page.mouse.move(g.plot.x + g.plot.width / 2, g.plot.y + g.plot.height / 2);\n    await page.mouse.wheel(0, -200);\n    await settle(page);\n    const zoomed = await domain(page);\n    expect(zoomed[1]! - zoomed[0]!).toBeLessThan(full[1]! - full[0]!);\n    expect(await page.evaluate(() => window.scrollY)).toBe(0);\n    expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it('category bar, line and area charts have no zoom controls; a donut has none (1.0: no category zoom)', async () => {\n    // Interaction review part 3: the earlier test created only a bar.\n    for (const [kind, options] of [\n      ['bar', { data: ['a', 'b', 'c'].map((x, i) => ({ x, y: i + 1 })), x: 'x', y: 'y' }],\n      ['line', { data: ['a', 'b', 'c'].map((x, i) => ({ x, y: i + 1 })), x: 'x', y: 'y' }],\n      ['area', { data: ['a', 'b', 'c'].map((x, i) => ({ x, y: i + 1 })), x: 'x', y: 'y' }],\n      ['donut', { data: [{ l: 'a', v: 1 }, { l: 'b', v: 2 }], label: 'l', value: 'v' }],\n    ] as const) {\n      const page = await fixturePage();\n      await page.evaluate(async ({ kind, options }) => {\n        const chart = window.Axylo[kind]!('#chart', { title: 'Z', ...options });\n        window.charts.push(chart);\n        await chart.__bench.ready();\n      }, { kind, options });\n      for (const label of ['Zoom in', 'Zoom out', 'Reset zoom']) expect(await page.locator('#chart button', { hasText: label }).count(), `${kind} ${label}`).toBe(0);\n      await page.focus('#chart .axylo-proxy');\n      await page.keyboard.press('+');\n      expect(await page.evaluate(() => window.charts[0]!.diagnostics.map(d => d.code))).not.toContain('AX199');\n      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n    }\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('touch (spec I4)', () => {\n  it('a tap pins the tooltip and a tap elsewhere dismisses it; a one-finger vertical drag scrolls the page', async () => {\n    const page = await fixturePage({ hasTouch: true, css: 'body { height: 3000px; }' });\n    await make(page, 'trend');\n    const g = await geometry(page);\n    const x = g.plot.x + g.plot.width / 2;\n    await page.touchscreen.tap(x, g.plot.y + g.plot.height / 2);\n    await page.waitForTimeout(50);\n    expect(await floating(page).isVisible()).toBe(true);\n    await page.waitForTimeout(400);\n    expect(await floating(page).isVisible()).toBe(true);\ndescribe('pass 4: controller finding 17, zoom does not apply to a category axis in 1.0', () => {\n  const data = ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D'].map((x, i) => ({ x, y: i + 1 }));\n  for (const kind of ['line', 'area', 'bar'] as const) {\n    it(`${kind}: zoom(['B', 'C']) is a no-op reported as AX150; marks, ticks, lookup and controls unchanged`, () => {\n      const seen: Diagnostic[] = [];\n      const r = record(kind, { title: 'Z', data, x: 'x', y: 'y', onDiagnostic: (d: Diagnostic) => seen.push(d) },\n        { container: { width: 600, height: 300 } });\n      r.frames();\n      const before = { layout: r.layout, lookup: r.committed!.lookup, view: r.committed!.view, draws: r.draws.length };\n      expect(r.prepared.at(-1)!.zoom).toBe(false);\n      let zoomed = 0;\n      r.controller.handle.on('zoom', () => { zoomed += 1; });\n      r.controller.handle.zoom(['B', 'C']);\n      r.frames();\n      expect(seen.map(d => [d.code, d.field])).toEqual([['AX150', 'zoom']]);\n      expect(zoomed).toBe(0);\n      const c = r.committed!;\n      expect(c.view).toBe(before.view);\n      expect(c.lookup).toBe(before.lookup);\n      expect(c.zoomed).toBe(false);\n      expect(r.prepared.at(-1)!.zoom).toBe(false);\n      expect(r.draws.length).toBe(before.draws);\n      if (r.layout?.kind !== 'plot') throw new Error('expected a plot');\n      expect(r.layout.xTicks.map(t => t.label)).toEqual(['A', 'B', 'C', 'D']);\n      expect(r.layout).toBe(before.layout);\n    });\n  }\n\n  it('donut: the same AX150 for a zoom request', () => {\n    const seen: Diagnostic[] = [];\nimport { expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { sliceText } from '../../src/lookup/text';\nimport { chart, codes, committed, defaultMessages, message, expectGeometry, lastModel, marks, reading, rows, walk } from './model';\n\nit('F8 donut: slices start at twelve and run clockwise in input order; zero and null are listed without arcs', () => {\n  const r = chart('donut', [{ x: 'Retail', y: 3 }, { x: 'None', y: 0 }, { x: 'Unknown', y: null }, { x: 'Trade', y: 1 }]);\n  r.frames();\n  expect(codes(r)).toEqual([]);\n  const arc = marks(r, 'arcs')[0]!;\n  expectGeometry(Array.from(arc.angles), [0, 1.5 * Math.PI, 1.5 * Math.PI, 2 * Math.PI]);\n  expect(arc.fills.every(paint => paint.kind === 'series')).toBe(true);\n  expect(new Set(arc.fills.map(paint => JSON.stringify(paint))).size).toBe(2);\n  const { lookup, view, formatters } = committed(r);\n  if (view.kind !== 'donut') throw new Error('Expected a donut view');\n  expect(view.slices.map(slice => {\n    const { label, value, percent } = sliceText(view, slice, formatters);\n    return [label, value, percent];\n  })).toEqual([['Retail', '3', '75%'], ['None', '0', '0%'], ['Unknown', 'No data', null], ['Trade', '1', '25%']]);\n  const legendReadouts = walk(r).map(ref => {\n    if (ref.kind !== 'slice') throw new Error('Expected a donut slice');\n    const tooltip = lookup.tooltip(ref);\n    return [tooltip.title, tooltip.rows[0]?.value, tooltip.rows[0]?.percent];\n  });\n  expect(legendReadouts).toEqual([\n    ['Retail', '3', '75%'], ['None', '0', '0%'], ['Unknown', 'No data', null], ['Trade', '1', '25%'],\n  ]);\n  expect(rows(r).map(row => row.slice(0, 2))).toEqual([['Retail', '3'], ['None', '0'], ['Unknown', 'No data'], ['Trade', '1']]);\n  expect(reading(r, walk(r)[0]!)).toContain('3 (75%)');\n  expect(lastModel(r).summary).toContain('Retail: 3 (75%).');\n  expect(lastModel(r).summary).toContain('Trade: 1 (25%).');\n  expect(lastModel(r).note).toBeNull();\n});\n\nit('F8 donut: seven largest categories and Other (3) are drawn; all ten categories remain individually readable in the table', () => {\n  const data = [\n    { x: 'A', y: 2 }, { x: 'B', y: 13 }, { x: 'C', y: 1 }, { x: 'D', y: 12 }, { x: 'E', y: 11 },\n    { x: 'F', y: 10 }, { x: 'G', y: 9 }, { x: 'H', y: 8 }, { x: 'I', y: 7 }, { x: 'J', y: 3 },\n  ];\n  const r = chart('donut', data);\n  r.frames();\n  expect(codes(r)).toEqual(['AX121']);\n  const { lookup } = committed(r);\n  const labelAndValue = walk(r).map(ref => {\n    const datum = lookup.datum(ref)!;\n    return [datum.seriesLabel, datum.value];\n  });\n  expect(labelAndValue).toEqual([['B', '13'], ['D', '12'], ['E', '11'], ['F', '10'], ['G', '9'], ['H', '8'], ['I', '7'], ['Other (3)', '6']]);\n  const fractions = [0, 13, 25, 36, 46, 55, 63, 70, 76].map(value => value / 76 * 2 * Math.PI);\n  const arc = marks(r, 'arcs')[0]!;\n  expectGeometry(Array.from(arc.angles), fractions.slice(0, -1).flatMap((start, i) => [start, fractions[i + 1]!]));\n  expect(arc.fills.at(-1)).toEqual({ kind: 'token', name: 'muted' });\n  expect(rows(r).map(row => row.slice(0, 2))).toEqual(data.map(row => [row.x, String(row.y)]));\n  expect(reading(r, walk(r).at(-1)!)).toContain('Other (3)');\n  expect(lastModel(r).summary).toContain('Other (3): 6');\n});\n\nit('F8 donut: a negative value shows the error state and clears all arcs', () => {\n  const r = chart('donut', [{ x: 'A', y: 2 }, { x: 'B', y: 1 }]);\n  r.frames();\n  r.controller.handle.update({ data: [{ x: 'A', y: 2 }, { x: 'B', y: -1 }] });\n  r.frames();\n  expect(codes(r)).toEqual(['AX120']);\n  expect(marks(r, 'arcs')).toEqual([]);\n  expect(lastModel(r).message).toBe(defaultMessages.error);\n  expect(r.announcements).toEqual([defaultMessages.error]);\n});\n\nit('F8 donut: all-zero values show the empty state while the table retains both zero values', () => {\n  const r = chart('donut', [{ x: 'A', y: 0 }, { x: 'B', y: 0 }]);\n  r.frames();\n  expect(codes(r)).toEqual([]);\n  expect(marks(r, 'arcs')).toEqual([]);\n  expect(lastModel(r).message).toBe(defaultMessages.empty);\n  expect(lastModel(r).summary).toContain(defaultMessages.empty);\n  expect(rows(r).map(row => row.slice(0, 2))).toEqual([['A', '0'], ['B', '0']]);\n});\n\nit('F8 donut: exactly eight slices including zero and null keep both arcless categories readable', () => {\n  const r = chart('donut', [\n    ...Array.from({ length: 6 }, (_, i) => ({ x: 'Positive ' + i, y: i + 1 })),\n    { x: 'Zero', y: 0 }, { x: 'Missing', y: null },\n  ]);\n  r.frames();\n  expect(codes(r)).toEqual([]);\n  expect(marks(r, 'arcs')[0]?.angles).toHaveLength(12);\n  expect(rows(r).slice(-2).map(row => row.slice(0, 2))).toEqual([['Zero', '0'], ['Missing', 'No data']]);\n  expect(walk(r).slice(-2).map(ref => committed(r).lookup.datum(ref)?.seriesLabel)).toEqual(['Zero', 'Missing']);\n});\n\n// F8 was amended so only slices with an arc count toward the limit.\nit('F8 donut: zero and null slices stay separate and only positive slices count toward the limit', () => {\n  const positives = Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, i) => ({ x: 'Slice ' + i, y: i + 1 }));\n  const zero = { x: 'Zero', y: 0 };\n  const missing = { x: 'Unknown', y: null };\n  const r = chart('donut', [...positives.slice(0, 7), zero, missing]);\n  r.frames();\n  expect(codes(r)).toEqual([]);\n  expect(marks(r, 'arcs')[0]?.angles).toHaveLength(14);\n  expect(rows(r)).toHaveLength(9);\n  expect(rows(r).slice(-2).map(row => row.slice(0, 2))).toEqual([['Zero', '0'], ['Unknown', 'No data']]);\n  expect(walk(r).slice(-2).map(ref => committed(r).lookup.datum(ref)?.seriesLabel)).toEqual(['Zero', 'Unknown']);\n\n  const grouped = chart('donut', [...positives, zero]);\n  grouped.frames();\n  expect(codes(grouped)).toEqual(['AX121']);\n  expect(grouped.controller.handle.diagnostics[0]?.count).toBe(2);\n  // Seven individual arcs and the grouped arc are drawn. Zero remains an individual legend entry.\n  expect(marks(grouped, 'arcs')[0]?.angles).toHaveLength(16);\n  const labels = walk(grouped).map(ref => committed(grouped).lookup.datum(ref)?.seriesLabel);\n  expect(labels).toEqual([...positives.slice(2).map(row => row.x), 'Zero', message('otherSlices', { count: 2 })]);\n  expect(rows(grouped).map(row => row.slice(0, 2))).toEqual([...positives, zero].map(row => [row.x, String(row.y)]));\n});\n            const bottom = top + mark.xywh[i + 3]!;\n            expect(mark.variant).toBe(cell.value === null ? 'missing' : 'bar');\n            if (cell.value === null) {\n              expect(top).toBe(bottom);\n              continue;\n            }\n            const tip = cell.tip < cell.base ? bottom : top;\n            const base = cell.tip < cell.base ? top : bottom;\n            expect(tip).toBeCloseTo(y.map(cell.tip), 3);\n            expect(Math.abs(base - y.map(cell.base))).toBeLessThanOrEqual(1.001);\n            if (!cell.value) expect(top).toBe(bottom);\n          }\n        }\n      } else {\n        const bands = marks(r, 'area');\n        expect(bands).toHaveLength(4);\n        for (const mark of bands) {\n          const upper = points(mark.upper);\n          const lower = points(mark.lower);\n          expect(mark.runs).toHaveLength(8);\n          for (const [side, offset] of [['positive', 0], ['negative', 4]] as const) {\n            const [start, count, base, baseCount] = mark.runs.slice(offset, offset + 4);\n            expect([count, baseCount]).toEqual([records.length, records.length]);\n            expectGeometry(upper.slice(start!, start! + count!).map(p => p[1]), components.map(row => y.map(row[mark.series]![side])));\n            expectGeometry(lower.slice(base!, base! + baseCount!).map(p => p[1]),\n              components.map(row => y.map(row[mark.series - 1]?.[side] ?? 0)));\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }), { numRuns: 1_000 });\n  });\n\n  it(`F10 ${type}: a missing ${kind} component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete${type === 'compact' ? ' (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)' : ''}`, () => {\n    const r = chart(type, [\n      { x: 1, a: 5, b: -3, c: 4, d: -2 },\n      { x: 2, a: 5, b: -3, c: null, d: -2 },\n      { x: 3, a: 5, b: -3, c: 4, d: -2 },\n    ], options(kind), undefined, kind);\n    r.frames();\n    const { x, y } = axes(r);\n    if (kind === 'bar') {\n      const missing = marks(r, 'rects').find(mark => mark.series === 2 && mark.variant === 'missing');\n      expect(missing?.xywh).toHaveLength(4);\n      expectGeometry([missing!.xywh[1]!, missing!.xywh[3]!], [y.map(5), 0]);\n    } else {\n      const mark = marks(r, 'area').find(mark => mark.series === 2)!;\n      const middle = pixel(x, 2);\n      const ordinate = (xy: Float32Array) => points(xy).filter(p => Math.abs(p[0] - middle) < 0.001);\n      expect(ordinate(mark.upper).some(p => Math.abs(p[1] - y.map(5)) < 0.001)).toBe(true);\n      expect(ordinate(mark.lower).some(p => Math.abs(p[1] - y.map(5)) < 0.001)).toBe(true);\n    }\n    if (type === 'compact') {\n      expectCompact(r);\n      expect(lastModel(r).summary).toContain('incomplete');\n    } else {\n      expect(at(r, 2).rows.map(row => row.value)).toEqual(['5', '-3', 'No data', '-2']);\n      expect(rows(r)[1]).toEqual(['2 (incomplete)', '5', '-3', 'No data', '-2']);\n      const announced = reading(r, refAt(r, 2));\n      expect(announced).toContain(defaultMessages.incompleteStack);\n      const spokenTotals = announced?.split(defaultMessages.total)[1]?.split(defaultMessages.incompleteStack)[0];\n      expect.soft(spokenTotals?.match(/-?\\d+/g)?.map(Number)).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([5, -5]));\n      for (const [x, positive, negative] of [[1, 9, -5], [2, 5, -5]] as const) {\n        const total = at(r, x).total;\n        const totals = total?.match(/-?\\d+/g)?.map(Number);\n        expect.soft(totals, 'the mixed-sign stack readout gives both sides').toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([positive, negative]));\n      }\n      expect(lastModel(r).note).toBeNull();\n    }\n  });\n}\n3:**The release gate can pass with required behavior removed.** The motion tests disable animations while measuring them. The table tests accept values under the wrong column headers. The reference tests accept a chart with neither reference mark drawn. The distribution suite also passes declarations that fail in a NodeNext TypeScript consumer.\n7:### Findings\n9:**B** means the test can be cited for a criterion it does not establish. **M** means a major limitation. **m** means a narrower defect.\n11:1. **B · I5 · Reasoned. The screenshot helper suppresses the behavior under test.** Every motion screenshot passes `animations: 'disabled'`. Playwright fast-forwards finite CSS animations and transitions. A one-second entry fade or a transition under reduced motion can therefore produce equal screenshots. `createRaw` also waits for readiness and three frames before the “first” capture. The update test waits two frames, allows another 300 ms, and never requires the updated picture to differ from the old one. An ignored update passes. Capture with animations enabled from the first eligible paint, require the known new data to appear, and measure the 200 ms deadline, including the specified 24-chart change. [Screenshot helper](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:246) · [Creation wait](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:72) · [Motion tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:419)\n13:2. **B · Packed TypeScript API · Ran. A supported ESM consumer loses the public types.** Both supplied Bundler-mode projects compile. Running the npm fixture with `--module NodeNext --moduleResolution NodeNext --noEmit` produces TS2834 at lines 5 and 6 of the shipped `index.d.ts`, missing public exports, and unused `@ts-expect-error` directives. The React fixture also loses its core option types. The `types` condition is correctly first and `public.d.ts` ships. The failure is the extensionless `./public` inside the ESM declaration. Emit `./public.js` in those declaration references and compile minimal packed consumers in both resolution modes. [Public entry](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/index.ts:5) · [Fixture configuration](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/fixtures/npm/tsconfig.json:3) · [Type tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/types.test.ts:13)\n15:3. **B · DX7/P6 · Ran. The size measurement is reproducible, but CI succeeds over budget.** I recovered the original tarball from the local npm cache, verified its SHA-512 against the committed size record, and independently bundled its production ESM bytes with esbuild `write:false`. Everything measured **283,389 minified bytes, 100,093 gzip bytes, 97.75 KiB**. Line-only measured **282,947 / 99,956 / 97.61 KiB**. CI calls `size` without `--check`. Even with `--check`, the script compares rounded KiB, so 40 KiB plus one byte passes. Compare integer bytes against `targetKiB * 1024` and make that exit status part of the release gate. The later fixture currently on disk gives 98.44 KiB and has a different integrity hash. [Size comparison](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/size.mjs:64) · [CI invocation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/.github/workflows/ci.yml:44) · [Recorded artifact](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/bench/size-latest.json:4)\n17:4. **B · L2/A5 · Ran the colour math, reasoned about the browser assertions. The palette test measures CSS colours before painting.** `seriesColors` takes the first computed `color` per SVG slot and fills a separate one-pixel canvas with it. The background comes from a CSS variable. Making the marks nearly transparent, changing their actual fill, or covering them leaves those readings intact. L2 similarly walks ancestor background colours, misses a mark painted behind text, and can pass an empty axis-colour loop. The severity-1 Machado coefficients, sRGB decoding, linear-RGB multiplication, clamp and OKLab transform are correct. My primary-colour and white probes matched reference OKLab values. The helper computes the continuous result and omits the simulated-image byte rounding distinguished in decision 0003. Sample known mark interiors and their actual backdrops in both schemes, assert samples exist, and score both analytic and raster variants. [Palette test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:294) · [Colour source](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:276) · [L2](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:100) · [Math](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/vision.ts:11)\n19:5. **B · A5 · Ran the separator counterexample, reasoned about grayscale. Both perceptual thresholds can give false passes.** I fed `separated` a transition with 0.80 pixel of background coverage. It reported one transition and zero touching. Stacked bars have an additional geometry check. Grouped bars, areas and donuts lack that protection, and the four-slice test accepts three transitions, missing the closing seam. The 85% marker intersection-over-union threshold is invented. Identical shapes can produce different thresholded masks through luminance, subpixel alignment or nearby ink. Check a full CSS pixel normal to each boundary, including the closing seam, and calibrate raster tolerance with known-width controls. For grayscale, include identical-shape negative controls and verify that the crossing traces can be matched to their legend markers. [Coverage calculation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:178) · [Closing seam](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:265) · [Marker masks](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:335)\n21:6. **B · L1/L8/A6 · Ran the text helper, reasoned about layout. A chart can discard labels and still pass.** Removing date or numeric ticks leaves fewer boxes to collide. Only the bar fixture compares a category count. The suite does not establish remedy order, three-line wrapping, the rotation limit, middle truncation with recoverable full text, AX143’s suggestion, or unchanged orientation. I confirmed that two boxes overlapping by 1.1 px are ignored when they have the same owner. Tooltip/readout text is excluded. L8 accepts a visible multi-line summary and does not bracket the 120×80 plot boundary. A6 uses a 320 px Chrome viewport as the 400% proxy and checks spacing separately. Use generated labels with known identities, check clipping ancestors and the actual remedies, bracket the fallback dimensions, and repeat with browser zoom and a delayed font in the required engines. A sibling test already loads an offline font. [L1](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:49) · [Text exclusions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/text.ts:20) · [L8](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:419) · [A6](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:49) · [Offline font precedent](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/render/review.browser.test.ts:439)\n23:7. **B · I1 and pointer/tooltip cells · Reasoned. Late, obscuring or incomplete tooltips can pass.** Every probe settles before reading, so there is no input-to-paint p95 measurement. Scatter and donut supply `marks: []`, making their pointer occlusion assertion vacuous. Bars check only the top eight pixels. The hover test jumps into the tooltip and checks visibility without checking that the same datum stayed put. The narrow readout can drop all eight rows and retain `+2 more`. A scatter radius of 20 px can pass the tested inside offsets and 30 px miss. Exercise a slow pointer path, hit-test the tooltip, check the active mark and all row identities on both surfaces, bracket 24 px, and reverse source order in the tie fixture. Add horizontal bars, hidden area/bar series, and timestamped paints. [Pointer probes](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:37) · [Hover and readout](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:99) · [Scatter radius](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:88)\n25:8. **B · A1/A4 · Ran the text oracle, reasoned about the table. Correct words can be attached to the wrong thing.** Swapping North and South’s cells while retaining their headers passes `toContain` for each value. Missing scatter series and donut category/percentage headers can pass the header subset check. The range test omits zoomable bars, and the layout test uses two fixed-height charts instead of the specified 24. For A1, I passed every compact summary-fragment assertion with the overall range statement removed. With an author description, retaining only that text, the zone and the omission also passes. Compare ordered headers and exact ordered cell arrays, assert each named summary clause, and check a date-bar zoom and a 24-tile layout. The fixture formatter also turns `0.000123456` into `0.000123`, contrary to F6. Use hand-written boundary values. [Table expectations](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a4-table.browser.test.ts:86) · [Range cases](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a4-table.browser.test.ts:207) · [Summary assertions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a1-names.browser.test.ts:104) · [Fixture formatter](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/fixtures.ts:21)\n27:9. **B · A2/A7 and keyboard evidence · Reasoned. The tests can keep reading the old proxy after focus has gone elsewhere.** `valueText` reads the selected DOM element’s `aria-valuetext`. It never requires that element to be focused or exposed as a range. The focus-indicator test compares the tooltip with datum marks rather than the indicator. The streaming test uses a growing window while focused, strips position and donut percentage in one comparison, and omits donut from the stricter check. A stale proxy, a covered ring, or lost focus at eviction can pass. Assert the active element, its unignored AX role, numeric position and bounds, actual ring clearance, and the next navigation result before and after eviction. Keep the DOM value-text assertion explicitly labelled. [Value-text helper](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:182) · [Focus indicator](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a2-keyboard.browser.test.ts:246) · [Streaming focus](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:131)\n29:10. **B · L7/A7/I6 · Reasoned. State changes can reach the reader while the checked surface stays quiet.** L7 verifies one nonempty polite mutation on loading→ready. An unrelated announcement qualifies. Error and internal-failure messages need only differ or be nonempty, with no equivalent bounds, tick or announcement checks. A7’s observer misses a newly inserted, already populated alert whose parent is outside a live region. I6 freezes only SVG scene markup and checks a final row count. While paused, the summary, lookup or open table could advance, or Resume could duplicate one buffered row and lose another. Assert exact state text, geometry and notification sequence, and compare fixture values across the reader surfaces during pause and after resume. [State transitions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:383) · [Live observer](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:97) · [Pause test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:477)\n31:11. **B · A8 · Reasoned. “Every fixture in every state” exceeds what axe scanned.** The helper requests all default-enabled rules with no explicit rule disablement. Most runs are scoped to `#chart`. The additional `body` run retains only `heading-order`, and the suite discards `incomplete` results without requiring `scrollable-region-focusable` to complete. Hidden scatter series, paused charts, zoomed bars, compact area/bar and other fixtures are absent. The pointer-tooltip setup can also miss a scatter point or land in the donut hole without failing setup. Assert each state exists before scanning, enumerate applicable fixture/state pairs, and record completion of the named rules. Use a page with suitable landmarks for the document-level scan. [State selection and axe results](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:166) · [Axe configuration](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/util.ts:117)\n33:12. **B · A10 · Ran the key comparison, reasoned about coverage. “Every built-in string” has a concrete omission.** `seeTable` exists in the reviewed contract and is absent from `MESSAGE_KEYS` and the replacement placeholders. One `ZZ-` anywhere plus the absence of a short English blacklist is enough. Hard-coding `Resume`, for example, passes without entering the paused state. At `77213c0` the language test inspects `.axylo-summary`, while the figure actually references `.axylo-description`. Removing `lang` only from the referenced description can pass. Use a compile-time exhaustive message map, trigger each applicable string, and require its individual sentinel and language at the surface that exposes it. [Replacement and language tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:215) · [Public message](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/public.ts:204) · [Referenced description](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:200)\n35:13. **B · T-dense/C2 · Reasoned. A spike at the wrong x passes the dense line and area tests.** Both use one unstacked series and compare the globally highest stroke coordinate with a height calculated from the library’s own domain. Moving the spike to another column or drawing every sample passes. No cumulative stack, same-column break, dropped-but-reachable ordinary sample, DPR variation or compact simplification is established. The scatter test counts `M` commands and the donut test counts paths, so repeated geometry can stand in for missing marks. Derive expected per-column extrema and breaks from fixture coordinates at a fixed domain, check stacked cumulative values, and identify marks by location. [Dense tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:294) · [Compact fidelity cases](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts:78)\n37:14. **B · T-limit/F8 · Reasoned. The ninth series can reuse the first cue, and the wrong seven slices can be selected.** The test computes drawn identities but asserts only `drawn.length >= 9`. Multiple elements of one series count separately. Distinct legend SVG markup does not prove distinct painted cues. Every grouping fixture places the seven largest values first, so keeping the first seven passes. The ordinary order fixture is also descending, and the all-zero test accepts an arbitrary nonempty error message. Check eight without the limit warning and nine with it, associate one painted cue with each series, scramble slice magnitudes, and compare the exact grouped arc, legend, table and empty state. [Identity assertion](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:404) · [Donut grouping and empty state](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts:101)\n39:15. **B · L6/T-reference · Reasoned. Removing the reference drawing passes.** The four Cartesian cases verify a domain, label near a calculated line position, and words in the summary and caption. They never require the line or band to be painted. The band is inside the data extent, and its adjacent label is unchecked. The donut negative case likewise checks the label, description and diagnostic without inspecting for an unintended mark. Put each reference outside the original extent in turn, sample its geometry or pixels, and check each label against its own mark. [Reference cases](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:429)\n41:16. **B · F2/F12 · Reasoned. Comparing two renderings can preserve the same gap bug, and a changed-value note can say the wrong thing.** For regular dates, bridging both the null run and the deleted run passes the geometry-equality check. The rendered suite never requests `missing: 'zero'`. Scatter counts two marks without identifying them or checking the missing row in the table. The donut F2 body only reads the table. For changed values, `1 … table` satisfies the AX160 case without checking AX160 or the meaning of the note. The AX121 case likewise accepts a note saying the grouped values were lost. Assert independent gap/zero coordinates, the affected rows, the diagnostic, and exact changed-versus-omitted wording at the displayed revision. [Date gaps](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f2-gaps.browser.test.ts:74) · [Scatter and donut](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f2-gaps.browser.test.ts:144) · [Changed-value notes](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f12-note.browser.test.ts:89)\n43:17. **B · I2/I3/I4 · Reasoned. Several control paths can be disabled independently.** Space need only change AX `pressed`, with no post-Space mark check. Zoom out is never clicked, Meta-wheel is absent, and the default pinch can suppress browser zoom while leaving the chart domain unchanged. I4 measures visible buttons and inputs. Selectable tooltip rows are `div` elements and never enter that measurement. Touch exercises a datum and page scroll, leaving most controls unoperated by touch. Assert each control’s visible result with its actual input, check browser defaults and both modifiers, and measure clickable tooltip rows while displayed. Donut and compact are appropriately outside the series-toggle matrix. [Legend tests](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:200) · [Zoom and touch](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:307) · [Selectable rows](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/tooltip.ts:89)\n45:18. **B · L3/L4/L5 · Reasoned. The layout and theme observations permit stale marks.** L3 can resize the CSS box while retaining the old drawing, and never opens the auto-height table to check flow. L4’s dark fixture sets both scheme and text colour, so always choosing by text luminance can pass. It permits two animation frames and lacks independent runtime checks for the specified root attributes and media changes. L5 samples roughly 5.5 px and widely separated points. A 20 px cutoff can pass both. Check a known datum and hit target across resizes, open the table, deliberately put scheme and inherited colour in conflict, measure the first post-change paint, and bracket 12 px. [L3](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:159) · [L4](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:218) · [L5](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:281)\n47:19. **B · C1–C5 · Reasoned. Compact coverage does not transfer across implementations of the three variants.** The general `compact` fixture is a line. Disabling motion or theme updates only on compact area/bar escapes those loops. C1’s hover check only searches for two named surfaces on one tile. C2’s area can fill from a truncated domain minimum to the bottom and pass the vertical-extent check. C3 checks SVG dimensions and the existence of a series element, allowing stale internal geometry. C4 reads cues on the coloured group and misses child paint. C5’s signed corner distances accept a marker entirely outside the figure. Parameterize the relevant fixtures over all three kinds. Verify marks-only behavior, data-derived geometry at each size, child paint, the AX131 suggestion, and a visible corner marker contained within the figure. [Compact fixture](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/fixtures.ts:105) · [C1/C2](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts:54) · [C3/C4/C5](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts:130)\n49:20. **B · DX8 text insertion · Reasoned. The same payload in several fields lets one surface vouch for another.** Full visible titles get exact comparisons. Series names, categories, subtitle, field labels, units, tick and value formatters receive payloads, and a document observer detects the selected element types if inserted. But tooltip positives cover only line/bar, the line name can satisfy its formatter assertion, and a table caption can satisfy the whole-table regex while cells are blank. Area has no table-text positive assertion. There is no per-tick, per-unit, summary or exact `aria-*` assertion. Messages overrides and a dirty reader note are never exercised. Use a different inert markup-shaped sentinel for each source, trigger each destination, and assert exact literal text or attribute value plus absence of parsed descendants. [Inputs](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/pages/charts.ts:21) · [Surface assertions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts:92) · [Observer](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/pages/observe.js:9)\n51:21. **B · DX8 StrictMode and DX1 scope · Reasoned. A leaked first mount can leave the expected single figure.** The React fixture really enables development StrictMode, but the assertion sees only the eventual figure. Keeping the original subscription or observer alive through cleanup can pass. Observe setup, disposal, setup again and final unmount through the packed adapter, including whether the old handle still acts. The DX1 snippets demonstrate a first **line** chart by all three routes. Only npm is exercised without a title. A matrix that repeats those results for the other constructors needs corresponding minimal examples or an explicit package-level scope. DX10 coverage here ends at those three snippets. [StrictMode test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:113) · [Untitled test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:49) · [Snippet inventory](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/snippets.test.ts:13)\n53:22. **M · Fixture isolation and extraction · Ran resolution and archive probes.** Normal core imports resolve inside each fixture, and the React fixture resolves both packed packages. But the npm and script fixtures can import undeclared `@axylo/react` from root `node_modules`. I observed Node resolve `packages/react/dist/index.js`, esbuild pull in workspace React **and core source**, and TypeScript resolve an explicit adapter type reference to `packages/react/dist/index.d.ts`. The existing positive path checks catch several fallbacks in their specific projects. They do not isolate consumers. Put fixtures outside the workspace ancestry and share only declared third-party dependencies. The actual archives contained 10 and 6 regular files, with no links or extended names. The extractor handles ordinary ustar prefixes, GNU `L`, and simple local pax `path=` records. Splitting pax by newline breaks a length-prefixed path containing a newline, global headers are ignored, and symlinks are rejected. npm’s packlist excludes ordinary symlinks. Prefer the npm installation/extraction path or explicitly constrain and test the supported subset. [Fixture placement