cument that says there is no third-party code. Vendored code without a header passes, and properly attributed code fails. Pin observable development-only behavior independently of the guard syntax. Verify the release inventory and corresponding notices, retaining the mechanical checks for the shipped MIT file, dependencies and imports. [Development token oracle](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/conditions.test.ts:142) · [Licence assertions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/licence.test.ts:68)\n59:### Disposition of the 14 recorded failures\n63:| **A10, six types** | **Original product defect.** Built-in English summary sentences inherited German. The later figure code sets a language on both summary elements, and all six pass in the later run. Finding 12 limits what those passes establish. [Figure update](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:200) |\n64:| **A5, grouped bar** | **Original product defect under the ordinary reading of “adjacent filled marks.”** At the original revision each bar consumed the full group subdivision, leaving zero geometric gap. The reported 0.22 px is consistent with antialiasing at a touching edge. The later revision subtracts a pixel and the fixture passes. [Grouped widths](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:70) |\n65:| **C4, compact bar** | **Original product gap under A5; residual test defect at `77213c0`.** C4 literally specifies dashes for lines. Requiring a non-colour cue for compact bars is supported by A5. Originally neither of the first two series received a pattern. At `77213c0` the second does, and SVG paints it on child rectangles. The test skips children without their own inline series colour and compares `none\\|\\|` with `none\\|\\|`. Inspect the child fills or pixels before treating this as a product failure. [Pattern selection](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:106) · [SVG paint](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/render/svg.ts:410) |\n66:| **L1, line/area/scatter/donut at 200% text** | **Original product defects. Residual reader-visible clipping, with a misleading test diagnosis.** The original output includes full summaries and displaced controls. The later run reports only the first sentence at 240 px. The stylesheet now ellipsizes it, while `Range.getClientRects()` measures the underlying text. That output cannot establish painted ink outside the figure or vertical overflow. Independently, the four sentences measured **270, 276, 303 and 288 px** in local Noto Sans at the fixture’s 24.5 px summary size. Each exceeds 240 px. Under L1/L8 I would retain the reader-facing failure until a meaningful one-line summary fits, and change the test to distinguish clipping, ellipsis and actual overflow. [Summary CSS](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:122) · [Range measurement](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/text.ts:36) |\n67:| **I1, scatter** | **Original product defect.** The recorded misses include a probe inside the plot near the top-edge EU point. `43fc75d` corrected edge projection and grid-cell rounding. The later acceptance run passes. [Grid boundary handling](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:47) |\n68:| **I1, bar** | **Original product defect.** Seven in-viewport top-row probes produced a reader surface outside the viewport. That directly violates I1. The later placement changes pass this fixture. [Viewport assertion](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:82) · [Later run report](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:73) |\n70:### Accessibility, input and waits\n72:**Computed Chrome AX evidence** comes from `Accessibility.getPartialAXTree` and `getFullAXTree`. It covers A1 names/descriptions/heading levels, I2 pressed state, A4 table roles/names/rows/cells and region focusability, F12 note text, C1/C5 image descriptions, and parts of F2, F8, L7, L8, T-reference and A10. **DOM evidence** includes A2/T-keyboard/F2/A7 `aria-valuetext`, live-region mutation counts, nearest `lang` ancestors, and part of the jump-error description check. Those establish authoring or DOM behavior. They do not establish speech. The distribution `figureName` helper uses Playwright’s `ariaSnapshot`, a different mechanism from the CDP tree helper. [AX helpers](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/util.ts:138) · [Distribution name helper](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/browser.ts:166)\n74:I found **no DOM-dispatched synthetic pointer, touch, wheel or keyboard events** in the reviewed acceptance tests. Playwright supplies mouse, keyboard and tap input. Pinch and one-finger scroll use CDP `Input.dispatchTouchEvent`, which exercises Chrome’s input pipeline. Direct `.focus()` bypasses the route to focus, and `chart.zoom()` establishes state without exercising a reader control. Those are appropriate setup operations only when the route itself has separate evidence. Touch emulation provides no physical-phone or touch-screen-reader result. [Pinch](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:307) · [Touch scroll](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:385)\n76:I found **no timeout-to-skip path**. The catches after the F12 note, L3 reveal and I4 scroll waits are followed by assertions that fail if the state remains absent. They do allow a transient or substantially delayed success, and I4 should compare the post-drag scroll position with its immediate pre-drag position. The consequential timing loopholes are the multi-frame settle, disabled animations, and the longer observation deadlines. [Note wait](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f12-note.browser.test.ts:91) · [Reveal wait](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:205) · [Scroll wait](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:400)\n78:### The report’s ambiguity choices\n96:### Type-matrix disposition\n112:### Verification and areas found sound\n128:- **Colour arithmetic — ran.** Normal-vision OKLab reference values matched, and the severity-1 simulation uses the expected matrices and linear-light ordering.\n129:- **Input injection — reasoned.** The real-key, mouse, wheel and CDP touch paths are appropriate for the Chrome interactions they actually exercise.\n130:- **Table paging — reasoned.** All 250 row headers are compared across three pages, and the million-row line fixture independently expects `123.25` at x `900,123`.\n131:- **Node import and validation — ran.** Both packed core conditions loaded without a DOM, added no globals, and returned AX103 at row 3, AX106 at row 4 and AX102 at row 5.\n132:- **CSP delivery — reasoned.** All eight variants receive the strict response header and early event listener. The negative control exercises blocked inline script-attribute and style-attribute paths.\n133:- **Package metadata — ran and inspected.** The `files` lists include the required entries and current declaration closure. `types` precedes runtime conditions. `[\"*.css\"]` correctly preserves CSS as a bundler side effect, and the adapter’s `sideEffects: false` is consistent with its import behavior. The esbuild CSS test alone cannot validate webpack behavior.\n134:- **Download accounting — ran.** Browser ESM, ES2022, production/default export selection, esbuild minification and gzip level 9 reproduce the figures. Bundler rows count embedded CSS once. The documented script-tag page downloads both its JS and linked CSS, so counting both transfers is correct. The adapter-only figure excludes its peers.\n136:**Criteria I would leave open for at least one applicable type:** **L1–L8, I1–I6, A1, A2, A4–A8, A10, F2 rendered, F5 rendered, F8, F12, C1–C5**, and the partial type-matrix cells identified above. On distribution, **DX7/P6 fails its measured budgets; DX8 and DX11 are partial; DX1 is established only at the demonstrated first-chart scope; DX10 beyond the three snippets is open.** A3 and A9 were outside this review.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
