aration and the palette are checked. No assertion identifies each slice without color by mapping it to its text. / Rendered palette and dash checks use compact line. Compact bar fails the non-color cue check recorded under C4.  \nL2 Light and dark computed colors, font sizes and focus contrast are sampled. Text painted inside marks and its actual pixel background are unverified. / The fixture has no visible chart text, axes or focus. Its computed mark colors are checked against the resolved background, without a rendered-pixel contrast check.  \nL8 The Node model varies width, container height and caption height. A browser must establish the one-line summary and controls in the resulting figure.  \nL3 Width changes, automatic height and a hidden start are checked. The chart height response to an independent resize and the title/control/table flow are unverified.  \nL4 The DOM exercises one body class toggle (sampled after two frame callbacks) and initial forced-colors. It does not prove the one-frame bound for runtime media, html/body inline style and data-theme changes.  \nA6  Chrome checks 320 CSS px and text-spacing overrides. Firefox and Safari results are absent, and the Chrome fixture uses a narrow viewport rather than actual 400% browser zoom. \nI1 Placement, pointer input and Escape pass sampled checks. The suites do not measure p95 input-to-readout latency or verify hover persistence along a pointer path. / Placement and Escape are sampled. The donut has no forced narrow readout test or p95 input-to-readout measurement.  \nI2   Donut has a legend under F8 and the toggle rule does not exempt slices. Click, Enter, Space and the pressed state need a donut legend test.\nI3 The four mechanisms are exercised. The click sequence never activates Zoom out, and the wheel guard checks Ctrl only.  \nI4  Chrome touch emulation provides tap, scroll and target-size evidence. Real phones are needed for native touch behavior. \nA7 The browser checks live-region quiet and focus identity. The focused accessible name/value stability case excludes donut. / A quiet append is verified in all three Node variants. Browser live-region and 24-chart checks are pending. The point-focus requirement applies where the chart has point navigation.  \nI5 The current browser tests check first render, reduced motion and a 24-chart filter against the 200 ms budget. Current browser results are pending. / Current browser citations cover first render and the 200 ms update case in the tested compact fixture. A 24-chart compact filter run is unverified.  \nA8 Checks axe across the listed states for categorical bars. The continuous-axis bar’s zoomed state is outside these fixtures. / The axe fixtures exercise compact line. Compact area and bar are unverified across the same states.  \nA10 The tests supply every known override but scan only selected English strings and surfaces in the tested states. Per-message coverage, including unvisited controls and states, is incomplete.  \nF9 Rendered eight-color checks use compact line only, and the twelve-series case checks model bindings rather than distinct rendered combinations in every compact variant.  \nL5 Dense, sparse and isolated examples are checked. They do not straddle the provisional 12 px cutoff.  \nC2 Baseline, sorted geometry, dirty data and static behavior are covered. Dense rendered compact strokes, compact bar gap styling and live scheme transitions for all three variants remain open.  \nDX1 Only the line has documented first-chart snippets proven in all three packed installation modes.  \nDX2 The fixture compares one logical series and one bad row. Multiple-series layouts and diagnostics whose caller indexes differ by form remain unchecked.  \nDX3 Packed type fixtures check specific counterexamples for selected types. The full set of applicable typed and untyped counterparts is unverified for this type. / Packed fixtures check bad line fields, wide y with series and an inapplicable option. The typed text-value failure is exercised on bar, rather than along with the line runtime case.  \nDX4 Runtime diagnostics are sampled, with registry cases under F3. A documentation page and verified link for every code are still missing.  \nDX5 Sequences and cancellation are checked. Heap retention over 1,000 create–destroy cycles remains unmeasured under P7.  \nDX6 The model checks named colors against a changing series set. No 24-tile test establishes cross-chart color stability together with inherited font and color and documented CSS font and spacing overrides.  \nDX8 Packed CSP pages draw these charts and Node runs without DOM globals. React StrictMode replay and hydration are exercised only on Line.  \nDX10 The three first-chart examples compile or run as applicable. The rest of the runnable documentation has no corresponding CI build and render. / Packed consumer fixtures compile calls, without a CI build and render of the runnable documentation examples.  \nP1   No valid acceptance measurement. Earlier first-chart comparisons were exploratory.\nP2   No valid acceptance measurement at both point counts. See decision 0002 for limits of the comparisons.\nP3   No valid acceptance measurement of the specified task and presented-frame pacing workload.\nP4   No valid measurement of p95 input-to-matching-frame latency.\nP5   No valid acceptance measurement. The earlier 24-chart run showed fallback text and drew no marks.\nP6   No valid P6 budget run is recorded. The available packed size measurement and target verdict are under DX7.\nP7   No valid owned-bytes and 1,000-cycle heap measurement. The earlier dashboard memory run was voided.\nP8   No valid 40-tile main-thread measurement.\n    // Compact area and compact bar, stacked with a missing component: the summary says the stacks are incomplete.\n    for (const kind of ['area', 'bar'] as const) {\n      await fresh(kind, { compact: true, data: [{ x: 'a', s: 'P', y: 1 }, { x: 'b', s: 'P', y: 2 }, { x: 'c', s: 'P', y: 3 }, { 