{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '78,112p' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/tests-opus.review.md\nrg -n 'F2.*compact|compact.*bar|zero' packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f2-gaps.browser.test.ts\nsed -n '64,171p' packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\nsed -n '1,120p' packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\nsed -n '245,305p;319,352p' packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\nrg -n 'country|en-IN|de-DE|documentElement.lang|timezoneId' packages/axylo/test/browser tests/dist --glob '*.test.ts'\nrg -n '96|80|2 KiB' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/size.analysis.md\"","aggregated_output":"### The report’s ambiguity choices\n\n| Reading | Judgment |\n|---|---|\n| Space before unit; medium en-US dates | Reasonable English fixture conventions. The spec permits locale-appropriate presentation. The six-fractional-places helper is a separate error. |\n| Summary y range means observed data extrema | Appropriate for a reader asking what values occurred. Test an axis whose bounds differ from the data and require an identifiable range statement. |\n| Scatter “last” means greatest x | Consistent with x-ordered navigation. Use shuffled input and define the equal-x case. |\n| Donut summary gives each value and share | Appropriate for parts of a whole. Also cover grouping, omissions and zero/null slices. |\n| Unmatched table jump gets a visible error | Appropriate. Require the error to identify the field and be programmatically associated with it. |\n| Separator coverage ≥0.75 px | Lowers the explicit 1 px requirement. Antialiasing calls for calibration, not a smaller nominal gap. |\n| Grayscale overlap ≤85% | An unvalidated regression heuristic. It cannot decide whether a reader can follow the crossing lines. |\n| A focused range should not recount arrivals | Consistent with decision 0004 for an unchanged datum. DOM stability is measurable; actual announcements require rehearsal. |\n| AX160 and AX121 count as “changed” | AX121 changes the displayed grouping. AX160 changes the presentation of a value. A disclosure is defensible in both cases, with wording that explains what changed and preserves the distinction from lost data. |\n| Double the inherited font size for text-only zoom | Useful for reproducing a real layout defect. It leaves fixed-pixel text unchanged and cannot substitute for browser text zoom. |\n| Hover the tooltip in one pointer step | Lowers the bar. A reader must be able to move onto it continuously and keep the same content. Decision 0004 explicitly describes that path. |\n| Scatter x-only zoom preserves the y domain | A reasonable 1.0 reading. Confirm the displayed y ticks against a fixture whose visible y extrema change materially. |\n| Allow 300 ms for a 200 ms transition | Lowers the explicit deadline by 50%, before the initial frame waits and screenshot overhead. |\n\n### Type-matrix disposition\n\nThese judgments cover the tested default SVG renderer. A later canvas run had 135 failures, many arising from SVG-specific inspection. It supplies no equivalent canvas pass. [Renderer report](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:99)\n\n| Cell | Line | Area | Bar | Donut | Scatter |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Pointer picking | Nearest-x fixture established | Same | Vertical bands only | Slice, hole and outside exercised | 24 px boundary and tie independence open |\n| Tooltip content | Visible/hidden fixture established | Initial stack total only | Grouped fixture only | Label/value/share established | Coincident row identities open |\n| Keyboard order | Fixture ordinal text exercised | Same | Same for vertical categories | Slice order exercised | x-then-y order exercised |\n| Zoom | Positive zoom exercised | Positive zoom exercised | Category/date covered; numeric and instant eligibility open | Keys tested in a sequence that can cancel; check after each action | x-only domain behavior exercised |\n| Dense drawing | Per-column F5 open | Cumulative F5 open | Count and AX132 exercised | Path count only | Count and AX133 exercised; positions and slow-drawing advice open |\n| Limit | Nine-warning positive only | Same | Same | Sorted-only grouping; boundary open | Nine-warning positive only |\n| Reference | Geometry and band domain open | Same | Same | Rejection/text checked; unintended drawing unchecked | Geometry and band domain open |\n\nThe fixture values and basic arithmetic generally have identifiable sources. I found no basis for alleging that the author pasted browser output. The problematic oracles are identifiable without that allegation: sibling-derived geometry, equality between two potentially wrong outputs, development tokens inferred from current source, and fragment/count assertions that discard associations.\n\n### Verification and areas found sound\n2: * F2, rendered (spec 3.1): missing values are never drawn as zero and never bridged; an isolated value\n3: * between two gaps is a visible point; a missing bar shows a \"no data\" mark distinct from a zero bar;\n47:    it(`F2 ${type}: null values are gaps, never zero and never bridged, and the value isolated between two gaps is a visible point`, async () => {\n57:      // No vertex at x = 2 or x = 4 (not drawn as zero), none bridging them.\n102:describe(\"F2 missing: 'zero'\", () => {\n104:    it(`F2 ${type}: with missing: 'zero' on the field, an explicit null and an absent step are drawn at zero, on the zero baseline`, async () => {\n109:      await createRaw(page, type === 'compact' ? 'line' : type, { title: 'Counts', data, x: { field: 'day', type: 'date' }, y: { field: 'v', missing: 'zero' }, ...(type === 'compact' ? { compact: true } : {}) });\n112:        // Seven bands; at days 2 and 4 nothing rises above the baseline (a zero bar, not a gap mark).\n118:        const zero = Math.max(...v.map(p => p.y));\n119:        // The lowest vertices are the two zeros, at the bottom of a value axis that starts at zero.\n121:        expect(Math.abs(sorted[0]!.y - zero)).toBeLessThan(0.01);\n122:        expect(Math.abs(sorted[1]!.y - zero)).toBeLessThan(0.01);\n126:          expect(Math.abs(zero - (plot.y + plot.height))).toBeLessThanOrEqual(1);\n135:  it('F2 bar: a missing bar shows a \"no data\" mark at the baseline, distinct from a zero bar and from an empty band', async () => {\n137:    await createRaw(page, 'bar', { title: 'Missing and zero', data: [{ q: 'Q1', v: 10 }, { q: 'Q2', v: null }, { q: 'Q3', v: 0 }, { q: 'Q4', v: 20 }], x: 'q', y: 'v' });\n149:    const missing = await patch(c1 + step), zero = await patch(c1 + 2 * step);\n154:    for (let i = 0; i < missing.length; i += 3) if (distance([missing[i]!, missing[i + 1]!, missing[i + 2]!], [zero[i]!, zero[i + 1]!, zero[i + 2]!]) > 40) differing++;\n155:    expect(differing, 'the missing and zero bars look different').toBeGreaterThan(4);\n162:    it(`F2 ${type}: the tooltip, the table and the keyboard read \"No data\" at the missing value, and the zero next to it as 0`, async () => {\n172:      const zero = await valueText(page);\n173:      expect(zero).not.toContain('No data');\n174:      expect(zero).toMatch(/\\b0\\b/);\n185:  it('F2 scatter: a point with a missing y is not drawn (never at zero): the two drawn points are the ones at (1, 5) and (3, 7); the table lists the missing row as \"No data\"; the keyboard skips it', async () => {\n  it(`F7 ${type}: for any generated extents the automatic domain includes data and references and the zoom stays inside its governing domain`, () => {\n    for (const kind of compactKinds(type)) {\n      const value = fc.integer({ min: -1_000, max: 1_000 }).map(value => value / 10);\n      fc.assert(fc.property(value, value, value, fc.boolean(), (a, b, reference, authored) => {\n        const r = chart(type, [{ x: 2, y: a }, { x: 4, y: b }], {\n          x: { field: 'x', domain: authored ? [0, 10] : undefined }, reference: [{ x: 8, label: 'Deadline' }, { y: reference, label: 'Target' }],\n        }, undefined, kind);\n        r.frames();\n        const initial = axes(r);\n        const zero = type === 'bar' || type === 'area' || type === 'compact' && kind !== 'line';\n        const lo = Math.min(a, b, reference, ...(zero ? [0] : []));\n        const hi = Math.max(a, b, reference, ...(zero ? [0] : []));\n        expect(initial.y.domain[0]).toBeLessThanOrEqual(lo);\n        expect(initial.y.domain[1]).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(hi);\n        firstTicks(r, lo, hi);\n        if (initial.x.type === 'band') throw new Error('Expected a continuous x axis');\n        if (authored) expect(initial.x.domain).toEqual([0, 10]);\n        else expect(initial.x.domain[1]).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(8);\n        r.controller.handle.zoom([-20, -17]);\n        r.frames();\n        const view = committed(r).view;\n        if (view.kind === 'donut') throw new Error('Expected Cartesian view');\n        if (type === 'compact') expect(view.xDomain).toEqual(initial.x.domain);\n        else {\n          expect(view.xDomain[0]).toBe(initial.x.domain[0]);\n          expect(view.xDomain[1]).toBe(initial.x.domain[0] + 3);\n          expect(view.xDomain[1]).toBeLessThanOrEqual(initial.x.domain[1]);\n        }\n      }), { numRuns: 1_000, examples: [[0, -0.8, 0.1, false]] });\n    }\n  });\n\n  for (const [scale, full] of [['percent', 100], ['ratio', 1]] as const) {\n    it(`F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick`, () => {\n      for (const kind of compactKinds(type)) {\n        const small = 0.04 * full;\n        for (const maximum of [small, full / 2, full, 1.1 * full]) {\n          const minimum = -0.01 * full;\n          const r = chart(type, [{ x: 1, y: minimum }, { x: 2, y: maximum }], { y: { field: 'y', scale } }, undefined, kind);\n          r.frames();\n          const { domain } = axes(r).y;\n          const atFull = maximum >= full / 2 && maximum <= full;\n          expect(domain[0]).toBeLessThanOrEqual(minimum);\n          expect(domain[1]).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(maximum);\n          // [-1, 4] (or [-0.01, 0.04]) has exact endpoints on the first 1% ticks.\n          if (maximum === small) expect(domain).toEqual([minimum, small]);\n          firstTicks(r, minimum, maximum, atFull ? full : undefined);\n          if (atFull) expect(domain[1]).toBe(full);\n        }\n        const labelOnly = chart(type, pair(full / 2), { y: { field: 'y', label: 'Percent (%)' } }, undefined, kind);\n        labelOnly.frames();\n        expect(axes(labelOnly).y.domain[1]).toBeLessThan(full);\n      }\n    });\n  }\n}\n\nfor (const type of ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter'] as const) {\n  it(`F7 ${type}: for any generated reference extreme the automatic value domain ends at the first drawn tick that reaches it (reading: the tick is the one the reader sees)`, () => {\n    const value = fc.integer({ min: 5, max: 100 });\n    fc.assert(fc.property(value, value, fc.boolean(), (low, high, upper) => {\n      const reference = upper ? high : -low;\n      const r = chart(type, [{ x: 2, y: upper ? -low : -1 }, { x: 4, y: upper ? 1 : high }], { reference: [{ y: reference, label: 'Target' }] });\n      r.frames();\n      firstTicks(r, -low, high);\n    }), { numRuns: 1_000 });\n  });\n}\n\nit('F7 line: finite data spanning extreme magnitudes remains in the finite value domain', () => {\n  const exponent = fc.constantFrom(-300, -225, -50, 50, 225, 300);\n  fc.assert(fc.property(exponent, exponent, fc.double({ min: 1, max: 9, noNaN: true }), (lo, hi, factor) => {\n    const a = -factor * 10 ** lo;\n    const b = factor * 10 ** hi;\n    const r = chart('line', [{ x: 1, y: a }, { x: 2, y: b }]);\n    r.frames();\n    const { y } = axes(r);\n    expect(y.domain.every(Number.isFinite)).toBe(true);\n    expect(y.domain[0]).toBeLessThanOrEqual(a);\n    expect(y.domain[1]).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(b);\n    expectGeometry(points(marks(r, 'path')[0]!.xy).map(point => point[1]), [y.map(a), y.map(b)]);\n  }), { numRuns: 1_000 });\n});\nimport fc from 'fast-check';\nimport { expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { at, axes, chart, expectCompact, expectGeometry, lastModel, marks, pixel, points, reading, refAt, rows, defaultMessages } from './model';\n\nconst stacks = [['area', 'area'], ['bar', 'bar'], ['compact', 'area'], ['compact', 'bar']] as const;\nconst options = (kind: 'area' | 'bar') => ({ y: ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'], ...(kind === 'area' ? { stacked: true } : { layout: 'stacked' }) });\n\nfor (const [type, kind] of stacks) {\n  it(`F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums`, () => {\n    const value = fc.oneof(fc.integer({ min: -20, max: 20 }), fc.constant(0), fc.constant(null));\n    const cells = fc.tuple(value, value, value, value);\n    fc.assert(fc.property(cells, cells, ([a, b, c, d], [e, f, g, h]) => {\n      const records = [\n        { x: 1, a: 7, b: -4, c: 2, d: -3 }, { x: 2, a, b, c, d },\n        { x: 3, a: -6, b: 5, c: -8, d: 6 }, { x: 4, a: e, b: f, c: g, d: h },\n        { x: 5, a: 5, b: -3, c: 0, d: null },\n      ];\n      const r = chart(type, records, options(kind), undefined, kind);\n      r.frames();\n      const { x, y } = axes(r);\n      const components = records.map(row => {\n        let positive = 0;\n        let negative = 0;\n        return [row.a, row.b, row.c, row.d].map(value => {\n          const base = (value ?? 0) < 0 ? negative : positive;\n          if ((value ?? 0) < 0) negative += value!;\n          else positive += value ?? 0;\n          return { value, base, tip: base + (value ?? 0), positive, negative };\n        });\n      });\n      expect(y.domain[0]).toBeLessThanOrEqual(Math.min(...components.map(row => row[3]!.negative)));\n      expect(y.domain[1]).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(Math.max(...components.map(row => row[3]!.positive)));\n      const indexAt = (px: number) => records.findIndex(row => Math.abs(pixel(x, row.x) - px) < 0.001);\n      if (kind === 'bar') {\n        expect(marks(r, 'rects').reduce((n, mark) => n + mark.xywh.length / 4, 0)).toBe(records.length * 4);\n        for (const mark of marks(r, 'rects')) {\n          for (let i = 0; i < mark.xywh.length; i += 4) {\n            const cell = components[indexAt(mark.xywh[i]! + mark.xywh[i + 2]! / 2)]![mark.series]!;\n            const top = mark.xywh[i + 1]!;\n            const bottom = top + mark.xywh[i + 3]!;\n            expect(mark.variant).toBe(cell.value === null ? 'missing' : 'bar');\n            if (cell.value === null) {\n              expect(top).toBe(bottom);\n              continue;\n            }\n            const tip = cell.tip < cell.base ? bottom : top;\n            const base = cell.tip < cell.base ? top : bottom;\n            expect(tip).toBeCloseTo(y.map(cell.tip), 3);\n            expect(Math.abs(base - y.map(cell.base))).toBeLessThanOrEqual(1.001);\n            if (!cell.value) expect(top).toBe(bottom);\n          }\n        }\n      } else {\n        const bands = marks(r, 'area');\n        expect(bands).toHaveLength(4);\n        for (const mark of bands) {\n          const upper = points(mark.upper);\n          const lower = points(mark.lower);\n          expect(mark.runs).toHaveLength(8);\n          for (const [side, offset] of [['positive', 0], ['negative', 4]] as const) {\n            const [start, count, base, baseCount] = mark.runs.slice(offset, offset + 4);\n            expect([count, baseCount]).toEqual([records.length, records.length]);\n            expectGeometry(upper.slice(start!, start! + count!).map(p => p[1]), components.map(row => y.map(row[mark.series]![side])));\n            expectGeometry(lower.slice(base!, base! + baseCount!).map(p => p[1]),\n              components.map(row => y.map(row[mark.series - 1]?.[side] ?? 0)));\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }), { numRuns: 1_000 });\n  });\n\n  it(`F10 ${type}: a missing ${kind} component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete${type === 'compact' ? ' (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)' : ''}`, () => {\n    const r = chart(type, [\n      { x: 1, a: 5, b: -3, c: 4, d: -2 },\n      { x: 2, a: 5, b: -3, c: null, d: -2 },\n      { x: 3, a: 5, b: -3, c: 4, d: -2 },\n    ], options(kind), undefined, kind);\n    r.frames();\n    const { x, y } = axes(r);\n    if (kind === 'bar') {\n      const missing = marks(r, 'rects').find(mark => mark.series === 2 && mark.variant === 'missing');\n      expect(missing?.xywh).toHaveLength(4);\n      expectGeometry([missing!.xywh[1]!, missing!.xywh[3]!], [y.map(5), 0]);\n    } else {\n      const mark = marks(r, 'area').find(mark => mark.series === 2)!;\n      const middle = pixel(x, 2);\n      const ordinate = (xy: Float32Array) => points(xy).filter(p => Math.abs(p[0] - middle) < 0.001);\n      expect(ordinate(mark.upper).some(p => Math.abs(p[1] - y.map(5)) < 0.001)).toBe(true);\n      expect(ordinate(mark.lower).some(p => Math.abs(p[1] - y.map(5)) < 0.001)).toBe(true);\n    }\n    if (type === 'compact') {\n      expectCompact(r);\n      expect(lastModel(r).summary).toContain('incomplete');\n    } else {\n      expect(at(r, 2).rows.map(row => row.value)).toEqual(['5', '-3', 'No data', '-2']);\n      expect(rows(r)[1]).toEqual(['2 (incomplete)', '5', '-3', 'No data', '-2']);\n      const announced = reading(r, refAt(r, 2));\n      expect(announced).toContain(defaultMessages.incompleteStack);\n      const spokenTotals = announced?.split(defaultMessages.total)[1]?.split(defaultMessages.incompleteStack)[0];\n      expect.soft(spokenTotals?.match(/-?\\d+/g)?.map(Number)).toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([5, -5]));\n      for (const [x, positive, negative] of [[1, 9, -5], [2, 5, -5]] as const) {\n        const total = at(r, x).total;\n        const totals = total?.match(/-?\\d+/g)?.map(Number);\n        expect.soft(totals, 'the mixed-sign stack readout gives both sides').toEqual(expect.arrayContaining([positive, negative]));\n      }\n      expect(lastModel(r).note).toBeNull();\n    }\n  });\n}\n    await createRaw(page, fn, { compact: true, title: 'Compact', data: variant === 'dirty' ? [{ d: 'a', v: 1 }, { d: 'b', v: '__NaN__' }, { d: 'c', v: 3 }] : [{ d: 'a', v: 1 }, { d: 'b', v: 2 }, { d: 'c', v: 3 }], x: 'd', y: 'v' });\n  } else await create(page, type, {}, '#chart', variant);\n}\n\ndescribe('A8 axe-core', () => {\n  for (const type of [...TYPES, 'compact area', 'compact bar'] as Kind[]) {\n    it(`A8 ${type.startsWith('compact') ? 'compact' : type}: axe-core reports no violations on the whole landmarked page in every state (${type}: ${states(type).map(s => s.name).join(', ')}, and with values left out), each state checked to hold before the scan`, async () => {\n      const failures: string[] = [];\n      const cases: [string, 'default' | 'dirty', State][] = [...states(type).map(s => [s.name, 'default', s] as [string, 'default', State]), ['values left out', 'dirty', states(type)[0]!]];\n      for (const [name, variant, state] of cases) {\n        const page = await landmarkPage();\n        await make(page, type, variant);\n        await state.enter(page);\n        if (!(await state.holds(page))) failures.push(`${name}: the state was not entered`);\n        const result = await axe(page, 'body');\n        for (const v of result.violations) failures.push(`${name}: ${v.id} (${v.nodes.join(', ')})`);\n        // heading-order decided (passed or failed, not left incomplete) wherever the chart has a heading.\n        if (!type.startsWith('compact') && !result.ran.includes('heading-order')) failures.push(`${name}: heading-order did not complete`);\n        await closePage(page);\n      }\n      expect(failures).toEqual([]);\n    });\n  }\n\n  for (const type of FULL as Full[]) {\n    it(`A8 ${type}: with a 250-row table open, its scroll region scrolls and axe-core decides scrollable-region-focusable with no violation`, async () => {\n      const page = await landmarkPage();\n      const day = (k: number) => new Date(Date.UTC(2026, 0, 1) + k * 864e5).toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n      const long: Record<Full, [string, Record<string, unknown>]> = {\n        line: ['line', { title: 'Long', data: Array.from({ length: 250 }, (_, k) => ({ d: day(k), v: k })), x: { field: 'd', type: 'date' }, y: 'v' }],\n        area: ['area', { title: 'Long', data: Array.from({ length: 250 }, (_, k) => ({ d: day(k), v: k })), x: { field: 'd', type: 'date' }, y: 'v' }],\n        bar: ['bar', { title: 'Long', data: Array.from({ length: 250 }, (_, k) => ({ d: `c${k}`, v: k + 1 })), x: 'd', y: 'v' }],\n        scatter: ['scatter', { title: 'Long', data: Array.from({ length: 250 }, (_, k) => ({ x: k, y: k % 7 })), x: 'x', y: 'y' }],\n        donut: ['donut', { title: 'Long', data: Array.from({ length: 250 }, (_, k) => ({ l: `c${k}`, v: k + 1 })), label: 'l', value: 'v' }],\n      };\n      await createRaw(page, long[type][0], long[type][1]);\n      await button(page, 'View as table').click();\n      await settle(page);\n      expect(await page.locator('#chart .axylo-table-scroll').evaluate(el => el.scrollHeight > el.clientHeight)).toBe(true);\n      const result = await axe(page, 'body');\n      expect(result.violations.map(v => `${v.id} (${v.nodes.join(', ')})`)).toEqual([]);\n      expect(result.ran).toContain('scrollable-region-focusable');\n      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n    });\n  }\n});\n\n// ── A10 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * Every key of the public `Messages` (src/public.ts). Typed as a record over its keys, so a key added to the\n * contract and missing here does not compile. Each entry names the chart types whose reader surfaces show\n * that string in the scenarios below, or says why none does.\n */\nconst WHERE: Record<keyof Messages, readonly ChartType[] | string> = {\n  viewAsTable: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], hideTable: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'],\n  noData: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], noObservation: ['line', 'area', 'bar'], incompleteStack: ['area', 'bar'],\n  moreRows: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter'], otherSlices: ['donut'], valuesNotShown: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'],\n  valuesChanged: ['donut'], labelsHidden: 'only when labels do not fit after every remedy; not reached by these fixtures',\n  loading: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'], empty: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'],\n  error: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'], internalError: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut', 'compact'],\n  position: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'donut'], total: ['area', 'bar'], panLeft: ['line', 'area', 'scatter'], panRight: ['line', 'area', 'scatter'],\n  // totalMixed: a mixed-sign stack's readout (spec F10). incompleteAt and incompleteCount are summary templates\n  // for charts that have no tooltip or table, the compact kinds (src/reader/index.ts uses them there); on full\n  // area and bar charts an incomplete stack is marked through incompleteStack in tooltip, table and value text.\n  // The compact scenario below exercises compact area and compact bar for them.\n  totalMixed: ['area', 'bar'], incompleteAt: ['compact'], incompleteCount: ['compact'],\n  jumpNotFound: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], plotInstructions: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'], seeTable: ['line', 'area', 'bar', 'scatter', 'donut'],\n};\nconst KEYS = Object.keys(WHERE) as (keyof Messages)[];\n/** Each key's own sentinel, with every placeholder the templates use, so filled templates stay recognisable. */\nconst sentinel = (k: keyof Messages) => `[${k}]`;\nconst MESSAGES = Object.fromEntries(KEYS.map(k => [k, `${sentinel(k)} {count}{seeTable}{type}{x}{y}{series}{value}{index}{label}{from}{to}{zone}{min}{max}{last}{total}{xLabel}{xMin}{xMax}{yLabel}{yMin}{yMax}{seriesCount}{values}{position}{percent}{example}{page}{positive}{negative}{at}`])) as Record<keyof Messages, string>;\n\n/** Everything the reader gets from the chart now: AX names, descriptions, roles, static text, the value text (DOM attribute), visible text and title attributes. */\nasync function surfaces(page: Page): Promise<string> {\n  const parts: string[] = [];\n  for (const n of await axWithin(page, '#chart')) parts.push(n.name, n.description, String(n.props.roledescription ?? ''));\n  parts.push(await page.evaluate(() => [...document.querySelectorAll('#chart *')].map(e => `${e.getAttribute('aria-valuetext') ?? ''} ${e.getAttribute('title') ?? ''}`).join(' ')));\n  parts.push(await page.locator('#chart').innerText());\n  return parts.join(' | ');\n}\n\n/** Scenarios that between them bring every applicable built-in string of `type` onto a reader surface. */\nasync function exercise(page: Page, type: ChartType): Promise<string> {\n  const seen: string[] = [];\n  const fresh = async (fn: string, options: Record<string, unknown>) => {\n    await page.evaluate(() => { for (const c of (window as unknown as { charts: { destroy(): void }[] }).charts.splice(0)) c.destroy(); });\n    await createRaw(page, fn, { ...options, messages: MESSAGES });\n  };\n  const take = async () => { seen.push(await surfaces(page)); };\n  const aligned = type === 'line' || type === 'area' || type === 'bar';\n  const fn = type === 'compact' ? 'line' : type;\n  const compact = type === 'compact' ? { compact: true } : {};\n  const DAY = 864e5, T0 = Date.UTC(2026, 2, 2);\npackages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts:172:    await page.evaluate(() => { document.documentElement.lang = 'de'; });\npackages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts:191:    await page.evaluate(() => { document.documentElement.lang = 'de'; });\npackages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:225:    await page.evaluate(() => window.charts[0]!.update({ y: { field: 'y', unit: 's' }, locale: 'de-DE' }));\npackages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts:589:    await page.evaluate(() => { document.documentElement.lang = 'de'; });\npackages/axylo/test/browser/chart/data.browser.test.ts:152:    for (const timezoneId of ['UTC', 'America/Los_Angeles', 'Asia/Kolkata']) {\npackages/axylo/test/browser/chart/data.browser.test.ts:153:      const page = await chartPage({ timezoneId });\npackages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review5.browser.test.ts:216:    await page.evaluate(() => { document.documentElement.lang = 'en'; });\npackages/axylo/test/browser/chart/review5.browser.test.ts:226:    await page.evaluate(() => { document.documentElement.lang = 'de'; });\n1:<!-- Analyst: Codex gpt-6.2-sol, effort max (observed in the session rollout, thread 01a1ed40-1abb-7cc2-8049-290d1bed775e), read-only. Source snapshot 8ab0734 per the analysis. -->\n3:**Keep the feature set and reset DX7.** I would set the next packed-distribution gates at **96 KiB for everything, 80 KiB for `line`, and 2 KiB for the React adapter**. Those are proposed gates. The measured line-only scratch bundle reached **79.79 KiB** with both renderers, streaming, zoom, the table, and keyboard support still in the bundle. With lazy loading, **93 KiB everything and 77 KiB line** are defensible *initial-download* gates. The original 40/25 KiB targets imply a substantially smaller product.\n14:| Packed, `validate` alone | 73,998 | 25,556 | 24.96 |\n28:| **Interaction** · 22,278 B | `present` ≈1,342, `build` ≈1,156, `onProxyKey` ≈1,083, `controlItems` ≈882, `placeProxy` ≈880. The shared state links pointer, touch, keyboard, focus, and the displayed revision. | Stubbing `present` removes 1,325 B. Stubbing the whole interaction factory removes 14,272 B including its dependencies. [Factory](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:150) · [Presentation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:360) · [Keyboard](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:543) |\n29:| **Aligned streaming** · 18,633 B for `store.ts` | `appendInPlace` ≈2,561, `commitBatch` ≈1,664, `batch` ≈1,380, `trim` ≈1,128, `extendSeries` ≈1,062. The shared stream row and aligned buffer modules contribute another 5,944 and 3,307 B respectively. | `appendInPlace` and `batch` ablations each remove about 1,050 B in separate builds. Cutting streaming end to end removes 13,692 B from everything and 11,138 B from the specialized line scratch bundle. [Batch](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:624) · [Append](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:895) · [Row revisions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-rows.ts:275) · [Frame buffers](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:23) |\n30:| **Point and donut streaming** · 7,806 B | `UnalignedStore` ≈3,509, `Points` ≈1,757, `Slices` ≈1,228. The first is shared by the last two. An aligned chart has no use for these classes. | The entire module disappeared from the line scratch metafile once `openStore` directly selected `AlignedStore`. [Point storage](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts:87) · [Slice storage](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts:175) · [Store constructors](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts:424) |\n32:| **Layout and time** · 7,273 B label fitting, 3,461 B layout, 5,107 B time scale | `layoutAxes` ≈1,689, `fitBottom` ≈1,296, `middleText` ≈838. Time-scale `label` and `wallBoundaries` are each ≈660, and the `SUB_YEAR` interval table is ≈543. | Stubbing `fitBottom` removes 720 B. Stubbing temporal ticks, readouts, gap arithmetic, and zone conversion together removes 3,442 B and breaks F2/F4/F6. [Layout](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/layout/index.ts:129) · [Labels](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/layout/labels.ts:363) · [Time intervals](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scale/time.ts:51) |\n53:I tested the dependency result with an in-memory `export { line }` entry. I folded the relevant chart-kind and frame-shape branches to line, replaced `openStore` with a direct aligned call, and removed the unreachable mark cases in each backend. This measured **81,704 gzip B (79.79 KiB)** with both renderers, down **18,032 B**. SVG alone measured **80,321 B (78.44 KiB)**. The metafile confirmed that point/donut stores, the scatter grid and point order, all scatter/donut lookup, and bar/area scene modules disappeared. This models the code the composition can omit. A production refactor will have dispatch and packaging overhead of its own.\n67:| 7 | **Defer plot keyboard navigation.** Stubbing the proxy handlers, placement, and navigation entry points saved **1,446 B**. I estimate **800–1,200 B** net after a synchronous shell and loader. | **Keep eager for the first release.** The proxy supplies native focus and screen-reader input, and shares the active datum with pointer and streaming. Deferring the first keystroke or announcement is a material regression. Check A2–A3, A7, A10 and I3. Medium to large. [Proxy creation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:220) · [Proxy keys](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:543) · [Revision remapping](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1252) |\n75:The duplication audit also found distinct checks that should stay distinct. `sameValue` compares option content recursively, `sameKey` compares stage inputs, and the store tests whether a normalized seed is reusable. Field checks recur against initial data, re-encoded retained data, and incoming rows. The `validateOptions` helper in `data/validate.ts` contributes zero bytes, so deleting it would save zero. Text uses DOM setters, and I found no duplicated general-purpose HTML escaping pipeline. The table’s two regex escapes are local to parsing a localized jump value. [Option equality](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/options.ts:66) · [Cache keys](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:246) · [Seed check](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:30) · [Retargeting](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/options.ts:196) · [Append field check](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:904) · [Unused validator](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/validate.ts:6) · [Table parser](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:997)\n87:| **Eager restructuring, full behavior** | **94–97 KiB estimated** | **76–81 KiB estimated** | Medium-high. Type composition alone should leave everything near the current size. The combined CSS, bench, and shorter-hint scratch variants measured **95.16 / 77.42 KiB**. The range allows for real composition and packing overhead. |\n91:The old targets are **unsuitable for the required release scope**. A single combined cut that removed streaming, table and plot keyboard behavior, tooltip, zoom, key temporal paths, scatter picking, and Canvas still weighed **67.06 KiB everything / 54.96 KiB line**. Even a one-shot SVG scratch entry that took raw inputs and retained normalization, validation, axis fitting and CSS, while leaving out the chart controller and reader interactions, measured **45.41 / 38.80 KiB**. To ship at 40/25 with this architecture, the product would also have to narrow or delegate input handling and axis behavior. Requiring prepared numeric or category data, with application-owned temporal parsing, diagnostics and accessible readouts, is an example of a scope that fits. It gives up parts of F3–F4, A1–A4, DX2–DX5 and I6. [Release scope](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:46) · [Pipeline and fidelity](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:169)\n106:| 6. **Release coordinator** · Measure the packed npm, IIFE and React cases and freeze DX7. | Proposed gates **96/80/2 KiB** eager, or **93/77 KiB** for initial npm downloads if the lazy split ships. | Run the full unit and browser suites, including the 494 Node acceptance cases in the cited run, and feed their results to the release checker. Record initial and all-chunk totals separately. [Acceptance runner](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/acceptance/README.md:3) · [Archived Node acceptance result](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:96) |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '298,373p;446,491p' packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts\nsed -n '120,210p' packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts\nrg -n '900,000|900_000|1,000,000|1_000_000|millio|inherited.*font|font.*inherited|pinned|24.*color' packages/{axylo,react}/test --glob '*.test.ts'\nrg -n 'browser|title' acceptance/run.mjs | tail -20\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '298,373p;446,491p' packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts\nsed -n '120,210p' packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts\nrg -n '900,000|900_000|1,000,000|1_000_000|millio|inherited.*font|font.*inherited|pinned|24.*color' packages/{axylo,react}/test --glob '*.test.ts'\nrg -n 'browser|title' acceptance/run.mjs | tail -20\"","aggregated_output":"describe('L3 the chart follows its container', () => {\n  for (const type of FULL as Full[]) {\n    it(`L3 ${type}: resized 720 → 360 → 720 px with no call from the page, the marks are redrawn for each width: a known datum sits at the same share of the plot, and pointing at it there shows it`, async () => {\n      const page = await devPage();\n      await create(page, type);\n      const shares: number[][] = [];\n      for (const w of [720, 360, 720]) {\n        await setWidth(page, w);\n        expect((await box(page, '#chart svg.axylo-svg')).width).toBeLessThanOrEqual(w + 0.5);\n        const p = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-proxy');\n        const d = await thirdDatum(page, type);\n        shares.push([(d.x - p.x) / p.width, (d.y - p.y) / p.height]);\n        await page.mouse.move(d.x, d.y + (type === 'donut' ? 4 : 0));\n        await settle(page);\n        const tip = (await page.locator('#chart .axylo-tooltip, #chart .axylo-readout').allTextContents()).join(' ');\n        // The third mark by x: Mar 4 (line, area), Q3 (bar), EU's third point at 30 kB (scatter), the first slice (donut).\n        const want = { line: 'Mar 4, 2026', area: 'Mar 4, 2026', bar: 'Q3', scatter: '30 kB', donut: 'Travel' }[type];\n        expect(tip, `${w} px`).toContain(want);\n        await page.mouse.move(0, 0);\n      }\n      // The datum keeps its place (for a donut, its angle on a ring that is re-centred, so the share of\n      // the plot's width moves with the ring's size and only the return to 720 px is compared).\n      if (type !== 'donut') expect(Math.abs(shares[1]![0]! - shares[0]![0]!)).toBeLessThan(0.03);\n      expect(shares[2]).toEqual(shares[0]);\n      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n    });\n\n    it(`L3 ${type}: with no definite height the plot is 16:9 of its width, clamped to 160–480 px, stable over 10 frames; an opened table flows in the figure and pushes nothing over the next element`, async () => {\n      const page = await devPage({ viewport: { width: 1300, height: 1400 }, css: '#chart { height: auto; }' });\n      await create(page, type);\n      for (const w of [240, 720, 1200]) {\n        await setWidth(page, w);\n        const heights: number[] = [];\n        for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) { heights.push((await box(page, '#chart .axylo-plot')).height); await frames(page, 1); }\n        const plot = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-plot');\n        const expected = Math.min(480, Math.max(160, (plot.width * 9) / 16));\n        expect(Math.abs(heights[0]! - expected), `${w} px wide`).toBeLessThanOrEqual(1);\n        expect(new Set(heights.map(h => Math.round(h))).size).toBe(1);\n      }\n      await page.locator('#chart [role=\"toolbar\"] button', { hasText: 'View as table' }).click();\n      await settle(page);\n      const fig = await box(page, '#chart figure');\n      expect(inside(await box(page, '#chart .axylo-table'), fig)).toBe(true);\n      const after = await box(page, '#after');\n      expect(after.y).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(fig.y + fig.height - 1);\n      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n    });\n\n    it(`L3 ${type}: a container that starts hidden draws when it is shown, at the shown size`, async () => {\n      const page = await devPage({ css: '#chart.off { display: none; }' });\n      await page.evaluate(() => document.querySelector('#chart')!.classList.add('off'));\n      const { fn, options } = optionsFor(type);\n      // Created while hidden: nothing can be drawn yet, so the test does not wait for a drawn frame here.\n      await page.evaluate(({ fn, options }) => {\n        const w = window as unknown as { Axylo: Record<string, (t: string, o: unknown) => unknown>; charts: unknown[] };\n        w.charts.push(w.Axylo[fn]!('#chart', options));\n      }, { fn, options });\n      await page.evaluate(() => new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100)));\n      await page.evaluate(() => document.querySelector('#chart')!.classList.remove('off'));\n      await page.waitForFunction(() => [...document.querySelectorAll<SVGElement>('#chart svg.axylo-svg .axylo-scene *')].some(e => /--axylo-series-color-/.test(e.style.getPropertyValue('color'))), null, { timeout: 5000 }).catch(() => undefined);\n      await settle(page);\n      const p = await box(page, '#chart .axylo-proxy');\n      expect(p.width).toBeGreaterThan(300);\n      const d = await thirdDatum(page, type);\n      expect(inside({ ...d, width: 0, height: 0 }, p, 8), 'the datum is drawn inside the shown plot').toBe(true);\n      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n    });\n  }\n});\n\n// ── L4 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/** The colours the marks are painted with now: computed colour of each series' first scene element. */\nasync function markColors(page: Page): Promise<string[]> {\n  return page.evaluate(() => {\n    const seen = new Map<number, string>();\n      for (const [label, on, off] of triggers) {\n        const now = await firstFrameAfter(page, on);\n        expect(now, `${label}: dark in the first frame`).not.toEqual(L);\n        D ??= now;\n        expect(now, label).toEqual(D);\n        await settle(page);\n        const pixel = await firstMarkPixel(page, type);\n        const [want] = await resolveColors(page, [D[0]!]);\n        expect(pixel, `${label}: painted`).not.toBeNull();\n        expect(Math.max(...pixel!.map((v, i) => Math.abs(v - want![i]!)))).toBeLessThanOrEqual(24);\n        expect(await firstFrameAfter(page, off), `${label} removed`).toEqual(L);\n        await settle(page);\n      }\n      // A media change: a chart that follows the device (color-scheme: light dark) on a dark device.\n      await page.evaluate(() => document.querySelector('#chart')!.classList.add('follow'));\n      await settle(page);\n      await page.emulateMedia({ colorScheme: 'dark' });\n      await frames(page, 1);\n      expect(await markColors(page), 'prefers-color-scheme: dark').toEqual(D);\n      expect(await closePage(page)).toEqual([]);\n    });\n\n    it(`L4 ${type}: a light-only page on a dark device stays light, and --axylo-background overrides the detected scheme`, async () => {\n      const page = await devPage();\n      await create(page, type);\n      const light = await markColors(page);\n      await page.close();\n      const device = await devPage({ colorScheme: 'dark' });\n      await create(device, type);\n      expect(await markColors(device)).toEqual(light);\n      await closePage(device);\n      const dark = await devPage({ css: DARK_PAGE });\n      await create(dark, type);\n      const darkMarks = await markColors(dark);\n      await dark.close();\n      const override = await devPage({ css: '#chart { --axylo-background: #101010; }' });\n      await create(override, type);\n      expect(await markColors(override)).toEqual(darkMarks);\n      expect(await closePage(override)).toEqual([]);\n    });\n\n    it(`L4 ${type}: in forced-colors mode the marks are painted in system colours, also when it is switched on at run time`, async () => {\n      const page = await devPage({ deviceScaleFactor: 2 });\n      await create(page, type);\n      await page.emulateMedia({ forcedColors: 'active' });\n      await settle(page);\n  });\n});\n\n/** The computed dash of each stroked series line, in slot order. */\nasync function strokeDashes(page: Page, selector = '#chart'): Promise<string[]> {\n  return page.evaluate(selector => {\n    const out: [number, string][] = [];\n    for (cons